#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "aebe3048-cc5b-5340-a15e-d577ae2ee72a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5479" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n![](images/36/36c1ce5342657231cd78154ab4821a6a5bf9b78b74297ae5a4cdccdc2f6d5dcd.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/1c/1cab5be2ed7c560a3a5192473be4ff7b6cf6dc5728552f1d179c73affebefe20.svg)\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4\\cdot 3 & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092075 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/id #uuid "55e695b2-4581-5ba7-9604-506234b88323" :question/math-academy-id "e-5480" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](images/2c/2c669dd6f7c5fa368c5ea28961d2ef57cac9deaf7ba453f75a441b05206f6276.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/e4/e4e91261ec7f4a9a48847005a57730afa25f5e69a1f3818ad583acaadae639f8.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation. \n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/id #uuid "a42d0af8-869c-5c2a-8182-22b14b9546e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5481" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](images/9f/9f13c3379e0613ce91669f6e52473dd11dc95360c422943764f30220dbccf430.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿![](images/03/039ee6073538580614cc07453132b811a4da81f438abf37197bb686057b4b66c.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-3\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ 70-7\\lambda -10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-17\\lambda +52 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{(-17)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =13,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9e40836e-18e9-5df6-a930-05875b920335" :question/math-academy-id "e-5482" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](images/e3/e34b5bf690a1dd8f5275f2d742b264494386b95394bc7c32aaafb9eeba68e058.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/37/37f547d6ad345415a1cc2480adf227ec29e31a351cf935e584b9544e44347310.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )-9\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues $\\lambda={\\color{red}3}$ and $\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}.$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix ![](images/f4/f4e86a797cafe4857d5f135ec37d57e33368469767e50793f55b89ec7185c2eb.svg)\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426470 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab8fa77-b07d-58b9-9474-d0c32cc4c09f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426442} {:answer/id #uuid "1fdedc73-108d-54bf-a80b-6f8d76425d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426443} {:answer/id #uuid "21d98a0f-7b72-5084-9fcf-ee900921103a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426444} {:answer/id #uuid "719faad2-519c-564b-8cd3-1c5984c43468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426446} {:answer/id #uuid "91ad27ae-e7c0-5e02-81e4-7e77b33fc829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21d98a0f-7b72-5084-9fcf-ee900921103a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426444} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce446c5-2796-5a84-9642-b7abdb29a329" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9582a502-0045-5277-be86-c165d61a4715" :question/math-academy-id "q-106983" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-2\\cdot (-2) & =0 \\\\ 4-\\lambda -4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-5)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =25-32 \\\\  & =-7 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1579836b-928d-5630-a28f-d0c7c7253871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda )(3+\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426441} {:answer/id #uuid "9013b695-47d7-5345-8e34-adeef9ec45a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426450} {:answer/id #uuid "a6fcae26-6730-5f46-b148-3f49f85151c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{5}+\\lambda )(3+\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426455} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6c3991-2598-5cbe-9812-a3bee7a1a7b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda )(3+\\lambda )=3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426457} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2114a5-18f4-5f18-bee2-e633eb8f49ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )=3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1579836b-928d-5630-a28f-d0c7c7253871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda )(3+\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426441} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6f044b9-2809-589e-a726-05924b47253a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dca9fe6d-d02a-5d80-b4d4-5f9b25f0fbc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-36766" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\sqrt{5}-\\lambda )(3+\\lambda ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ad3afc0-1147-5a90-b327-46c419abae45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =7$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402511} {:answer/id #uuid "bebf86c2-9d02-56e0-8de7-e3c093fdb99b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402512} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe3b5b3-5b53-5af3-a386-d1a9cac7570e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402513} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1b2964-fbf6-54e9-a3dc-5eb4004c5b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =7$ and $\\lambda =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402514} {:answer/id #uuid "00de227b-1e08-5a35-a745-88b3e218426e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fe3b5b3-5b53-5af3-a386-d1a9cac7570e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402513} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c905a94-1e61-56fb-85f0-520ef6a3631a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fda33b2-0f78-5ef6-abce-da9e465c13f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-36780" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-1\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ 49-7\\lambda -7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +54 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-14)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 54 \\\\  & =196-216 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $P$ does not have real eigenvalues."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a127b5d-b607-5917-a20b-32fd0f904754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426440} {:answer/id #uuid "73fdf196-1f18-59d1-ae5d-7f8ae207a749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda +1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426447} {:answer/id #uuid "759d3da2-313d-516d-b70d-7d701f27b667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda -1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426448} {:answer/id #uuid "c3759497-c425-5fbe-9add-59747632a611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda -1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426456} {:answer/id #uuid "d23dbfdf-5925-53a9-aa26-ace0d4372cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d23dbfdf-5925-53a9-aa26-ace0d4372cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426459} :answer-field/id #uuid "a405d6cc-14d9-5743-9f23-3b29719764ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0cba12d-30e2-5e4e-9717-4d5124d428a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-76341" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $L=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{5}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{5}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\frac{1}{5}-\\lambda )-(-1)\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2} & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}\\lambda  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a25f6950-9088-5ff9-8175-877d50a81da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426452} {:answer/id #uuid "a4036eef-ab8d-5137-83eb-70652e3c8c6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426453} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c7c087-5672-5851-ae11-572422abc236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426458} {:answer/id #uuid "d5281683-5678-50f6-a3d4-31872aa9352f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =-\\frac{5}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426460} {:answer/id #uuid "f7818e8c-878b-5236-95a6-67cb75479fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4036eef-ab8d-5137-83eb-70652e3c8c6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426453} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ff870f2-a00f-5d9f-a34a-712ea4371cad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95fd78c2-6907-5df8-b9fe-1452968ce01b" :question/math-academy-id "q-76362" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )(\\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c33ad59-d29c-5cbd-910f-497a62d62bfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426445} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3b9b16-d329-5f89-9cff-6f464c33458f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426449} {:answer/id #uuid "a48e2962-ae97-5ce4-aaf1-eea3d88ff322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426454} {:answer/id #uuid "e26ddd9b-b057-5d08-b037-5d67a039567e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426461} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7bf537-28bf-51b9-a386-11e70b5bae0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c33ad59-d29c-5cbd-910f-497a62d62bfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426445} :answer-field/id #uuid "021cb7e9-9e31-5b4e-91d4-a97f82fcb114" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aaa6413c-ed34-5909-9e88-242b0b85efde" :question/math-academy-id "q-9339" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(B-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =1.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27ca6789-a24a-5ec2-9232-86bc94dc9daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354999} {:answer/id #uuid "2e864f43-7357-599c-9a27-32f22c394e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355067} {:answer/id #uuid "31107606-ccb7-5d05-8596-4e5888c1144b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =-9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355094} {:answer/id #uuid "897b443b-8095-5fdd-8fd7-f8556f4d4d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =5$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355882} {:answer/id #uuid "bd6f96b4-1d8f-51e8-b377-5e6a706e3f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd6f96b4-1d8f-51e8-b377-5e6a706e3f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356323} :answer-field/id #uuid "44285aea-3536-59ba-a136-9c87d9d92638" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bbc0e33-82aa-5775-853a-c2bdd5e62b0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9340" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-7\\cdot 7 & =0 \\\\ 4-2\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -45 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 45}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{196}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 14}{2} \\\\  & =-5,9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "616d5508-8a25-5988-bb35-0e6edabd52b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355531} {:answer/id #uuid "84cf261d-40c2-521f-8a39-62ae3d4837d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355836} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf397ea-4249-5ec0-9158-e941aa14ba00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356309} {:answer/id #uuid "d61eee99-b39f-5bb9-952c-e406a93f7b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356541} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c54bc1-9006-5edf-ad18-da9b6f40136b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbf397ea-4249-5ec0-9158-e941aa14ba00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356309} :answer-field/id #uuid "e23650fa-a017-55d4-aa2b-e248a6298430" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9a0d751-b8e6-598d-8c36-71f74a16fdfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-9348" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ -2+\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-3,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4.$"}]}
